+
+## System dependency probes (added by plan figure-out-way-to-install U4)
+
+`hive doctor` opens its row set with `kind: "dependency"` rows probing
+the operator machine (no project config required):
+
+| Tier | Rows | Behavior |
+|------|------|----------|
+| hard | `system/git`, `system/bash` | missing → status `missing`; `hive init` aborts pre-scaffold with the actionable install hint (distro-aware via `/etc/os-release`). |
+| warn | `agent/claude`, `agent/codex`, `agent/pi`, `github/gh`, `tooling/jq` | missing → status `warning` with hint; never blocks. claude/codex/pi also enforce their README version floors (`version_too_old`). |
+
+Policy: **report-with-hints, never auto-install.** The prompt installer
+(U11) consumes `hive doctor --json`; `jq` is a warning-level convention
+hint only — hive itself never invokes it.
+
 ## Row kinds
 
 `Doctor#call` builds two row kinds and concatenates them:
